# check register of the tests. Written by checks/check_register.py --record; do not edit.
# Not seen: an assertion in a branch never taken (if (false), Python if False:), a return or continue before an assertion,
# a lambda or nested def that is never called, a limit computed while a test runs from data (a function's result, a file
# the test reads, a number written in a string), a macro or monkey-patch defined outside tests/, limits in src/ (the
# verdict limits, the settings hash), the meaning of a test. The executed counts of tools/step_checks.py catch whole
# cases that do not run, not assertions inside a case.
# totals: 299 cases (7 should_fail, 28 skip), 1955 assertions, 250 python tests
# assertions by macro: CHECK 1499, CHECK_FALSE 105, CHECK_MESSAGE 12, CHECK_NOTHROW 1, CHECK_THROWS_WITH_AS 1, FAIL_CHECK 1, REQUIRE 328, REQUIRE_FALSE 5, REQUIRE_MESSAGE 2, WARN_MESSAGE 1; 68 of them in asserting helpers; 166 calls of helpers, 1395 values, 623 loop lines, 1695 number lines; 47 built files; 689 python assertions
# python lines by kind: assert 706, call 111, default 24, guarded 26, loop 22, number 415, value 14

